# Spinner

Shows that something is loading when you cannot tell how long it will take. For a known amount of progress, use `Progress` instead. The root sets `role="status"` and is named "Loading" for screen readers.

<Demo />

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<script lang="ts">
	import { Spinner } from "#lib/components/ui/spinner/index.js";
</script>

<Spinner />
```

## Installation

```pm
npx remote0 add https://plainsv.com/r/spinner.json
```

## Label

Set `aria-label` to describe what is loading, such as `aria-label="Loading results"`. The spinning circle itself is hidden from screen readers.

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<Spinner aria-label="Loading results" />
```

## Button

Place a spinner before the label of a disabled button while an action runs. The default variant follows the surrounding text color, so it matches every button variant. Use `size="sm"` in small buttons and `size="xs"` in extra small ones.

<Demo section="button" />

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<script lang="ts">
	import { Spinner } from "#lib/components/ui/spinner/index.js";
	import { Button } from "#lib/components/ui/button/index.js";
</script>

<Button disabled><Spinner />Saving</Button>
<Button size="sm" variant="secondary" disabled><Spinner size="sm" />Processing</Button>
```

## Variants

Set `variant` to `default` or `destructive`. To use another color, set `color` on the spinner or its parent.

<Demo section="variants" />

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<Spinner variant="destructive" />
```

## Sizes

Set `size` to `xs`, `sm`, `md`, or `lg`. The default is `md`.

<Demo section="sizes" />

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<Spinner size="lg" />
```

## API

The `Spinner` props extend the native `span` attributes, and extra attributes pass through to the root. When the user prefers reduced motion, the spinner turns more slowly instead of stopping.

```ts title="index.ts"
interface Props extends CompProps<"span"> {
	/** Color of the spinner; `default` follows the surrounding text color */
	variant?: "default" | "destructive";
	/** Spinner size on the shared scale; defaults to `md` */
	size?: UiSize;
}
```
